  "summary": "Smartphone agents don't get better by processing more data. They improve by training on as many different apps as possible. The researchers behind OpenMobile-2 built an open training environment with more than 110 applications, including 35 replicas of popular apps. On real Android devices, their model scores highest among open agents, the authors say. The article OpenMobile-2 proves open-source smartphone agents can rival proprietary models appeared first on The Decoder .",
